;153mguess and do not act destructively. Wait for my answer.                                                                                                                           [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mOnce every target repository has its 009-select-stop worktree under C:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\009, end your turn with a short factual summary  [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mof what you did. That summary must NOT end with a question — only end with a question mark when you are genuinely asking me how to proceed with a real conflict per the rule      [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mabove.                                                                                                                                                                            [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mPROJECT CONTEXT FILES: this project keeps its documentation under documentation/; the documents in documentation/context/ are shared by every play and apply to all work. Read    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mALL of them before doing anything and make your work conform to them: documentation/context/vision.md (the problem, users, and product direction), documentation/context/tech.md  [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m(overall architecture plus the technology used in each repository). Only the Architect writes documentation/context/vision.md and documentation/context/tech.md; treat every      [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mother document as read-only reference the user maintains, and do not create, move or edit anything else under documentation/.                                                     [m
